The likely common case, where the field already has an explicit type, now returns first behind a `__builtin_expect` branch hint. The profile lookup moves to a separate cold path that reads `profile->fields` through a local pointer. All return values are unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```